#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:1
msgid "Animation Design Thinking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:3
msgid ""
"How to decide WHAT to animate and HOW to structure it — before writing "
"any code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:5
msgid "Should I animate this?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:7
msgid ""
"Not everything benefits from animation. Motion adds cognitive load. Bad "
"animation is worse than a good static diagram."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:9
msgid "**Animate when:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:10
msgid ""
"A sequence unfolds over time (algorithm steps, derivation, pipeline "
"stages)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:11
msgid "Spatial relationships change (transformation, deformation, rotation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:12
msgid "Something is built from parts (construction, assembly, accumulation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:13
msgid "You're comparing states (before/after, method A vs method B)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:14
msgid ""
"Temporal evolution is the point (training curves, wave propagation, "
"gradient descent)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:16
msgid "**Show static when:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:17
msgid ""
"The concept is a single labeled diagram (circuit, anatomy, architecture "
"overview)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:18
msgid "Motion would distract from spatial layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:19
msgid "The viewer needs to study it carefully (dense table, reference chart)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:20
msgid "The concept is already intuitive from a well-labeled figure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:22
msgid ""
"**Rule of thumb:** If you'd explain it with \"first X, then Y, then Z\" —"
" animate it. If you'd explain it by pointing at parts of one picture — "
"show it static."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:24
msgid "Decomposing a concept into animation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:26
msgid "Step 1: Write the narration first"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:28
msgid "Before any code, write what the narrator would say. This determines:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:29
msgid "**Order** — what concept comes first"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:30
msgid "**Duration** — how long each idea gets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:31
msgid "**Visuals** — what the viewer must SEE when they HEAR each sentence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:33
msgid ""
"A scene where the narration says \"the gradient points uphill\" must show"
" a gradient arrow at that moment. If the visual doesn't match the audio, "
"the viewer's brain splits attention and both tracks are lost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:35
msgid "Step 2: Identify visual beats"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:37
msgid ""
"A \"beat\" is a moment where something changes on screen. Mark each beat "
"in your narration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:46
msgid ""
"Each beat is one `self.play()` call or a small group of simultaneous "
"animations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:48
msgid "Step 3: Choose the right tool per beat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "Visual need"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "Manim approach"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "Object appears for first time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "`Create`, `Write`, `FadeIn`, `GrowFromCenter`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "Object transforms into another"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "`Transform`, `ReplacementTransform`, `FadeTransform`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "Attention drawn to existing object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "`Indicate`, `Circumscribe`, `Flash`, `ShowPassingFlash`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "Continuous relationship maintained"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "`add_updater`, `always_redraw`, `ValueTracker`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "Object leaves the scene"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "`FadeOut`, `Uncreate`, `ShrinkToCenter`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "Static context that stays visible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "`self.add()` (no animation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:59
msgid "Pacing: the universal mistake is too fast"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:61
msgid "Timing rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "Content type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "Minimum on-screen time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "New equation appearing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "2.0s animation + 2.0s pause"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "New concept label"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "1.0s animation + 1.0s pause"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "Key insight (\"aha moment\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "2.5s animation + 3.0s pause"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "Supporting annotation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "0.8s animation + 0.5s pause"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "Scene transition (FadeOut all)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md
msgid "0.5s animation + 0.3s pause"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:71
msgid "Breathing room"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:73
msgid "After every reveal, add `self.wait()`. The viewer needs time to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:74
msgid "Read the new text"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:75
msgid "Connect it to what's already on screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:76
msgid "Form an expectation about what comes next"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:78
msgid ""
"**No wait = the viewer is always behind you.** They're still reading the "
"equation when you've already started transforming it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:80
msgid "Tempo variation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:82
msgid "Monotonous pacing feels like a lecture. Vary the tempo:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:83
msgid "**Slow build** for core concepts (long run_time, long pauses)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:84
msgid ""
"**Quick succession** for supporting details (short run_time, minimal "
"pauses)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:85
msgid ""
"**Dramatic pause** before the key reveal (extra `self.wait(2.0)` before "
"the \"aha\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:86
msgid ""
"**Rapid montage** for \"and this applies to X, Y, Z...\" sequences "
"(`LaggedStart` with tight lag_ratio)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:88
msgid "Narration synchronization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:90
msgid "The \"see then hear\" principle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:92
msgid ""
"The visual should appear slightly BEFORE the narration describes it. When"
" the viewer sees a circle appear and THEN hears \"consider a circle,\" "
"the visual primes their brain for the concept. The reverse — hearing "
"first, seeing second — creates confusion because they're searching the "
"screen for something that isn't there yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:94
msgid "Practical timing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:106
msgid "Equation decomposition strategy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:108
msgid "The \"dim and reveal\" pattern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:110
msgid "When building a complex equation step by step:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:111
msgid ""
"Show the full equation dimmed at `opacity=0.2` (sets expectation for "
"where you're going)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:112
msgid "Highlight the first term at full opacity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:113
msgid "Explain it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:114
msgid "Highlight the next term, dim the first to `0.5` (it's now context)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:115
msgid "Repeat until the full equation is bright"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:117
msgid ""
"This is better than building left-to-right because the viewer always sees"
" the destination."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:119
msgid "Term ordering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:121
msgid ""
"Animate terms in the order the viewer needs to understand them, not in "
"the order they appear in the equation. For `E = mc²`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:122
msgid "Show `E` (the thing we want to know)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:123
msgid "Then `m` (the input)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:124
msgid "Then `c²` (the constant that makes it work)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:125
msgid "Then the `=` (connecting them)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:127
msgid "Architecture and pipeline diagrams"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:129
msgid "Box granularity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:131
msgid ""
"The most common mistake: too many boxes. Each box is a concept the viewer"
" must track. Five boxes with clear labels beats twelve boxes with "
"abbreviations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:133
msgid ""
"**Rule:** If two consecutive boxes could be labeled \"X\" and \"process X"
" output,\" merge them into one box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:135
msgid "Animation strategy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:137
msgid ""
"Build pipelines left-to-right (or top-to-bottom) with arrows connecting "
"them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:138
msgid "First box appears alone → explain it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:139
msgid "Arrow grows from first to second → \"the output feeds into...\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:140
msgid "Second box appears → explain it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:141
msgid "Repeat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:143
msgid ""
"Then show data flowing through: `ShowPassingFlash` along the arrows, or a"
" colored dot traversing the path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:145
msgid "The zoom-and-return pattern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:147
msgid "For complex systems:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:148
msgid "Show the full overview (all boxes, small)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:149
msgid "Zoom into one box (`MovingCameraScene.camera.frame.animate`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:150
msgid "Expand that box into its internal components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:151
msgid "Zoom back out to the overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:152
msgid "Zoom into the next box"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:154
msgid "Common design mistakes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:156
msgid ""
"**Animating everything at once.** The viewer can track 1-2 simultaneous "
"animations. More than that and nothing registers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:157
msgid ""
"**No visual hierarchy.** Everything at the same opacity/size/color means "
"nothing stands out. Use opacity layering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:158
msgid ""
"**Equations without context.** An equation appearing alone means nothing."
" Always show the geometric/visual interpretation first or simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:159
msgid ""
"**Skipping the \"why.\"** Showing HOW a transformation works without WHY "
"it matters. Add a sentence/label explaining the purpose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:160
msgid ""
"**Identical pacing throughout.** Every animation at run_time=1.5, every "
"wait at 1.0. Vary it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_animation-design-thinking.md:161
msgid ""
"**Forgetting the audience.** A video for high schoolers needs different "
"pacing and complexity than one for PhD students. Decide the audience in "
"the planning phase."
msgstr ""

